   What constitutes listening to criticism? Debating the basics? The
basics are debated every day on talk.politics.misc, alt.politics.libertarian,
and libernet-d. Unless someone has a radically different argument, why
should we listen to it for the 100th time? We are bombarded by alternative
viewpoints constantly by the media anyway.  That's the whole point
of the safe-haven concept, being able to discuss the finer details
without arguing the fundamentals. If you have some kind of criticism
of capitalism or cryonics or nanotech, where is it?

